# REAL KISS frames captured from direwolf 1.7, not hand-written.
# Produced by: gen_packets -> WAV -> raw 16-bit 44.1k PCM -> direwolf (stdin) -> KISS TCP (the port scripts/regen-aprs-fixture.sh sets)
# Source packets (docs/plans/APRS_CONTROL_PLAN.md P1):
#   KE8XYZ-9>APDW17,WIDE1-1:GATE 7K2M9                          (a command)
#   KE8XYZ-9>APDW17,WIDE1-1:!4129.96N/08141.66W>088/034 test    (a position beacon)
#   W8ABC>APDW17::KE8XYZ-9 :net tonight 8pm{01                  (a third-party message)
# Each line is one KISS frame: first byte is the KISS port/command nibble pair,
# the rest is the raw AX.25 frame. Captured rather than constructed BECAUSE a
# hand-written fixture only proves the parser agrees with whoever wrote it.
